{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > legs.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Reusable skills derived from public frames and clone experiments.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nfrom perception import arr, connected_components, replay, safe_step\n\n\ndef center_link_on_ring(env):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Place two swappable endpoints around an outlined midpoint target.\n\n    Black is the movable endpoint; clicking green swaps the endpoints.\n    The white marker tracks their integer midpoint. Verify a symmetric\n    placement on a clone before committing its three coordinate clicks.\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\n    frame = arr(env.frame())\n    endpoints = [b for b in connected_components(frame, colors=[0, 3])\n                 if b.area == 12 and b.size == (5, 5)]\n    if len(endpoints) \"'!= 2:\n        return\n    green = next(b for b in endpoints if b.color == 3)\n    swap = (6, int(green.centroid[1]), int(green.centroid[0]))\n    markers = connected_components(frame, colors=[15])\n    # The target is an outline of isolated white pixels. Exclude endpoint\n    # centers and the solid white midpoint marker.\n    outline = [b for b in markers if b.area == 1 and not any(\n        e.bbox[0] <= b.centroid[0] <= e.bbox[2]\n        and e.bbox[1] <= b.centroid[1] <= e.bbox[3]\n        for e in endpoints)]\n    if len(outline) < 4:\n        return\n    tx = round(sum(b.centroid[1] for b in outline) / len(outline))\n    ty = round(sum(b.centroid[0] for b in outline) / len(outline))\n    base = env.levels_completed\n    for dx, dy in [(8, 0), (0, 8), (-8, 0), (0, -8)]:\n        a, b = (tx + dx, ty + dy), (tx - dx, ty - dy)\n        if not all(2 <= x <= 61 and 2 <= y <= 61\n                   and frame[y, x] != 2 for x, y in (a, b)):\n            continue\n        # Stage an endpoint near the target, swap to hold it fixed, then\n        # reduce midpoint distance to zero with the symmetric endpoint.\n        path = [(6, *a), swap, (6, *b)]\n        trial = replay(env, path)\n        if trial.levels_completed > base:\n            for action in path:\n                if env.terminal() or env.levels_completed > base:\n                    break\n                safe_step(env, action)\n            return\nPY\ncat > players.py <<'\"'PY'\n# Per-level players only compose reusable legs.\nfrom legs import center_link_on_ring\n\n\ndef play_level_1(env):\n    center_link_on_ring(env)\nPY\ncat > midpoint_candidate.json <<'JSON'\n[[6,47,21],[6,27,59],[6,31,21]]\nJSON\ncat >> legs_log.md <<'MD'\n\nLevel 1: public-frame probes reproduced black endpoint (7,36), green\nendpoint (27,59), white midpoint (17,47), and outlined target (39,21).\nClicks on free space move black; clicking green swaps the two endpoints.\nRepeated clicks and clicks at (0,0) leave geometry unchanged. A click at\n(1,1), on color 2, also leaves geometry unchanged. Across multiple placements,\nthe marker follows the endpoints' integer midpoint. No autonomous geometry\nmotion was observed during repeated clicks.\n\nDense subgoals: stage an endpoint eight pixels from the target, swap to\nanchor it, then place the other endpoint symmetrically, taking midpoint\nerror to zero. Pristine clones verified both horizontal and vertical\nplacements complete level 1. The candidate horizontal path is preserved in\nmidpoint_candidate.json. Near placements also won, so exact tolerance is\nunmeasured; the leg uses an exact symmetric placement and verifies reward\non a clone before committing. No existing legs were available.\nMD\npython gkm_try.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
